# Beat 11 of grpconf/synopsis.md — 1:30, the finale.
#
# STATUS: merged into log-v2.script (synopsis open question 3).
#
# Beat 10 and beat 11 share a session because the overrides set in beat 10
# must still be in force for the export.  The last two steps of
# log-v2.script are the export and the round-trip narration.
#
# presentation.sh invokes log-v2.script; beat 11's shell commands
# (prototext encode + cmp) follow it as separate eval'd lines.
#
# If the sessions are ever split, move these steps here:
#
#   title: Byte-exact
#
#   steps:
#     - text: |
#         One question left.  We have read the payload, named its fields,
#         and pointed at four things standard tooling does not show.
#
#         Did we change any of it?
#
#         Press Enter to write the document out as plain text.
#       fold: ["/ 0"]
#       unfold: [/]
#       node: /
#       override: export $STAGE/boblog.prototext
#
#     - text: |
#         The round trip is one command in the shell:
#
#             prototext encode boblog.prototext -o roundtrip.pb
#             cmp boblog roundtrip.pb && echo identical
#
#         The leaked key survived.  It would not have survived
#         protoc --decode.
#
#         :quit, and we close on the shell.
#       fold: ["/ 0"]
#       unfold: [/]
#       node: /

title: Byte-exact (merged — see log-v2.script)

steps:
  - text: |
      This script is a placeholder.  The export beat is the final two
      steps of log-v2.script, which runs in the same session as
      beat 10 so the overrides stay in force.

      If you are seeing this, presentation.sh has been updated to invoke
      this file separately.  Move the last two steps of log-v2.script
      here and restore the separate session invocation.
    fold: ["/ 1"]
    node: /
